tinyexpr - expression parser used by the eval module (eval.c)

Upstream:  https://github.com/codeplea/tinyexpr
Release:   v1.1.1
Commit:    6d2233ce14dca063994708a91b3b98e24e8aa0c3
Licence:   zlib (see LICENSE)

LICENSE is copied unmodified from the release.  tinyexpr.c and tinyexpr.h
are copied from the release and modified for uvrgw (uvrgw.patch, changes
marked "uvrgw:" in the source):

  te_is_builtin()       tells whether a name is a built-in function or
                        constant.  eval.c uses it to reject value names
                        that would hide a built-in (tinyexpr looks up
                        variables first), so the list of built-ins is
                        only defined in tinyexpr.c.

Examples, tests and benchmarks are not included.

Updating tinyexpr: copy the new tinyexpr.c/h, then apply uvrgw.patch
(patch -p1 < uvrgw.patch in this directory).  If the patch is forgotten,
linking fails (undefined reference to te_is_builtin).  Update release and
commit above.

Compile options are set in the uvrgw Makefile (not in tinyexpr.c):
  -DTE_POW_FROM_RIGHT   '^' is right associative and binds tighter than
                        unary minus (-2^2 = -4, 2^3^2 = 512)
TE_NAT_LOG is not defined, so 'log' is log10.
